      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_a58cce0cc2b533fe7cc5e4d037358c8de5ad2b45f960418ecb733e05a6b0da94",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "Long-time averaging of the finite Dirichlet polynomial retains the multiplicative diagonal: two k-tuples contribute when their products agree. Repeated Perron variables then externalize the individual upper cutoffs, leaving a constrained multivariable Dirichlet series whose multiplicative structure can be studied separately.",
