    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_2b1f35eeec1cced1b51c379563f60115460b5e13e9c8eea6ba8aa7d5269bafeb",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "For the truncated zeta pseudomoment, the constrained Dirichlet series factors into a regular Euler product tending to the prime-dependent constant a_k and pairwise zeta factors whose poles leave the geometric leading contribution. That geometric contribution is vol(P_k), also the normalized large-size limit of truncated unitary characteristic-polynomial moments, so the arithmetic and unitary-geometric factors enter through distinct source-supported mechanisms.",
