    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_c9dbc3c47e76de2c18a78be152970371c73a05012f86e0abfe4b07575ad2d865",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Nonnegative matrices form a common representation whose row and column margins translate between three settings: secular-coefficient exponents give exact margins, monomials in the residual zeta contour integrand encode those margins, and Perron cutoffs turn them into upper-bound constraints. The resulting bounded-margin count G_k is both an exact truncated unitary moment and the lattice-point count of a dilated substochastic polytope, whose Ehrhart leading coefficient is vol(P_k).",
